'''Gannis Ducain''' was a [[Kajain'sa'Nikto]] [[Gender|male]] [[Smuggler|gunrunner]] who stole the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'' from [[Han Solo]], only to have it stolen from him later by the [[Irving Boys]]. He later had a change of heart from his less-than-noble ways and joined the [[Resistance]].

==Biography==
===Stealing the ''Falcon''===
{{Quote|Solo should really keep a closer eye on his possessions!|Gannis Ducain, in the ''Smuggler's Guide''|<ref name="Smuggler's Guide">''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide]]''</ref>}}
Gannis Ducain<ref name="Cross">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: Incredible Cross-Sections]]''</ref> was a [[Kajain'sa'Nikto]]<ref name="Grand Theft Falcon" /> [[Gender|male]]<ref name="Smuggler's Run" /> who worked as a [[janitor]] in [[Takodana Castle]] for [[Maz Kanata]]. [[Captain]] [[Han Solo]], in need of help due to his usual [[First Mate]] [[Chewbacca]] being busy with [[Chewbacca's family|family business]], hired Ducain to help with a job to the [[planet]] [[Christophsis]], taking him aboard the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'', which Ducain knew from its role in events before and during the [[Galactic Civil War]]. Although Solo had given the young man advice on choosing to fight for what was right in [[the galaxy]], Ducain in [[31 ABY]]<ref name="Date1">"Flight of the Falcon, Part 5: Grand Theft Falcon" takes place after the events of "[[The Crimson Corsair and the Lost Treasure of Count Dooku]]," as [[Kix]] is indirectly mentioned, but before [[Life Day 1|''Life Day'' 1]], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to c. [[31 ABY]]. "The Crimson Corsair and the Lost Treasure of Count Dooku" refers to the prologue as taking place 50 [[Standard year|years]] prior to the main story. The prologue takes place in between "[[The Wrong Jedi]]" and [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']], both of which are placed in [[19 ABY]] by ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''. Therefore the prologue takes place in 19 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]], and the main story takes place around 31 ABY. Therefore, "Flight of the Falcon, Part 5: Grand Theft Falcon" also takes place around 31 ABY.</ref> elected to steal the starship while Solo left to meet his contact, using the legendary [[freighter]] to make a name for himself as a [[Smuggler|gunrunner]].<ref name="Grand Theft Falcon" /> Ducain discovered the ''[[Smuggler's Guide]]'' previously owned by the [[Master Codebreaker]] in the ''Falcon'' and recorded acquisition of title in it.<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />

===Enemy of the First Order===
Ducain added a rotating core to the ship's gun well.<ref name="Cross" /> Gaining the help of a mysterious contact, his legend grew throughout the [[galaxy]] for [[Standard year|years]] until he met with his contact on the world of [[Vardos]]. Really an [[First Order officer|officer]] of the emerging [[First Order]], Ducain's contact attempted to recruit him to their emerging effort. Supposedly agreeing but really planning to run, Ducain believed he needed to return the ''Falcon'' to Solo, only to lose the ship<ref name="Grand Theft Falcon" /> and ''Smuggler's Guide''<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" /> to the [[Irving Boys]] before he had the chance.<ref name="Grand Theft Falcon" /> Nevertheless, after the ''Falcon'' was again stolen by [[junk boss]] [[Unkar Plutt]], Solo and Chewbacca recovered the ''Falcon'' after it had been taken by defecting [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]] [[Finn]] and the [[Force-sensitive]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]].<ref name="TFA">{{Film|VII}}</ref> In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="34 ABY Date Note">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' places the events of [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']] in [[34 ABY]]. [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']] takes place immediately after the end of ''The Force Awakens''.</ref> after Solo's [[death]] during the [[Battle of Starkiller Base]], Chewbacca started to fix the unadvised modifications made by Ducain whilst Rey was trained by [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]] on [[Ahch-To]].<ref name="The Last Jedi Novel">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: Expanded Edition]]''</ref>

[[File:HorizonBaseMission.jpg|thumb|right|175px|thumb|Ducain working with Finn.]]
During her search for the ''Falcon'', [[Bazine Netal]] was told by [[Lady]] [[Proxima]] to travel to [[Jakku]] to speak with Ducain about the [[Starship|ship]].<ref name="Lady and the Tramp">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=17|story=Flight of the Falcon, Part 4: Lady and the Tramp}}</ref> By the time Netal found him, Ducain had officially changed his ways and decided to join the [[Resistance]].<ref name="Grand Theft Falcon" /> Ducain eventually [[Battle for Horizon Base|accompanied]] Finn to [[Horizon Base]] to attempt to recruit the [[Oru resistance]]. They were found by stormtroopers, but managed to slip away. They were then captured by the Oru forces, but Finn and Ducain convinced them of the righteousness of the cause. [[Mezlo]] used a [[candori]] to aid their escape. Mezlo declined their offer to join, but affirmed that they are honorable and will join in the fight if called.<ref name="Battle for Horizon Base">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=32|story=The Battle for Horizon Base}}</ref>

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Ducain was first mentioned in the [[2015]] novel ''[[Smuggler's Run: A Han Solo & Chewbacca Adventure]]'',<ref name="Smuggler's Run" /> as part of [[Journey to Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]. His first appearance was in ''[[Star Wars Adventures]]'' comic book series.<ref name="Grand Theft Falcon" />

